<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  desktopAhaan entitlements — kept minimal. Every key below is required
  by a specific feature and would break it if removed. See docs/SECURITY.md
  for the full rationale.

  app-sandbox             always required — opts the process into the
                          macOS Sandbox so writes are confined to the
                          app's container and reads are gated by other
                          entitlements.
  network.client          ONLY for FreeOnlineTranslationProvider. The
                          user can disable online translation entirely
                          via Settings → "Dictionary Only (Offline Mode)"
                          which makes the app fully offline. NWPathMonitor
                          observation alone does NOT require this entitlement.
  files.user-selected.read-write
                          Needed for BOTH the "Open Image…" NSOpenPanel
                          (OCR picks an image to read) AND the
                          "Save PDF" NSSavePanel under Olympiad Tests
                          (the kid / parent picks a destination to
                          write the print-ready paper). 2026-06-06:
                          upgraded from `read-only` because NSSavePanel
                          requires the read-WRITE variant — `read-only`
                          alone hard-crashes the panel construction
                          (EXC_BREAKPOINT) with the diagnostic "your
                          app has the User Selected File Read
                          entitlement but it lacks User Selected File
                          Read/Write to display save panels". The
                          previous OCR-only use case still works under
                          read-write (it's a superset).
  device.audio-input      ONLY for SpeechRecognitionManager (microphone
                          dictation for translator + practice answers).
                          Paired with NSMicrophoneUsageDescription +
                          NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription in Info.plist
                          (configured via INFOPLIST_KEY_* build settings).
  temporary-exception.files.home-relative-path.read-write [ /Documents/ ]
                          pre-authorises read+write access to ~/Documents
                          so the kid's iMac never sees the TCC "would like
                          to access Documents folder" popup on first launch
                          after a rebuild. Not allowed on Mac App Store
                          submissions; fine for the single-user sideloaded
                          build. Remove this entitlement to restore the
                          prompt.
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.temporary-exception.files.home-relative-path.read-write</key>
	<array>
		<string>/Documents/</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
